  "narrative": {
    "intro": "Perimeter Solutions has $343M in federal contract obligations in FY2026 to date across 20 awards, with an average award size of $17.1M and year-over-year obligations up 7.5%. Perimeter Solutions' federal obligations have trended upward since FY23, moving from $89.9M in FY23 to $319M in FY25 and reaching $343M in FY26 to date. Perimeter Solutions received larger funding from two agencies in FY2026 to date, with the Department of Agriculture obligating $227M and the Department of the Interior obligating $116M. Perimeter Solutions' current-year totals are partial because FY2026 is fiscal year to date, and the note clarifies that listed award-value figures in largest-awards and expiring-contracts tables represent total contract values rather than obligations. Perimeter Solutions' award count and average award size reflect active federal buying patterns in the current fiscal year to date, and the provided figures show where obligations concentrated by agency and by year. Readers should treat FY2026 numbers as incomplete for the full fiscal year because the period is fiscal year to date.",
